{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Al Sade. Nice to meet you. You're new with us, right? Can you tell me your full name and date of birth?",
   "start": 0.08,
   "end": 7.02
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yeah, Kenji Watanabe. March 9th, 2011.",
   "start": 7.74,
   "end": 11.16
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Thanks, Kenji. Is apparent with you today.",
   "start": 11.94,
   "end": 14.02
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "My mom, Yumi. She's out in the car on a work call. She said I'm 15. I can handle it.",
   "start": 14.54,
   "end": 20.38
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Fair enough. So what happened to the ankle?",
   "start": 21.04,
   "end": 22.76
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I rolled it at basketball on Sunday. Wait, no, Saturday. It was Saturday morning practice. I went up for a rebound and came down on another guy's foot and it kind of turned in.",
   "start": 23.64,
   "end": 35.58
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Ouch, which ankle?",
   "start": 36.16,
   "end": 36.78
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Right one it swelled up right away. I limped off but I could walk.",
   "start": 37.56,
   "end": 41.4
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Did you hear a pop or a snap?",
   "start": 42.42,
   "end": 43.7
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No I don't think so.",
   "start": 44.32,
   "end": 45.44
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "How bad is the pain now, zero to ten?",
   "start": 46.46,
   "end": 48.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Like a six when I walk on it, maybe a two when I'm just sitting.",
   "start": 49.58,
   "end": 53.2
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any numbness or tingling in your foot?",
   "start": 54.05,
   "end": 55.97
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Nope.",
   "start": 56.99,
   "end": 57.15
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "any pain in your knee or higher up the leg no just the ankle what have you done for it so far",
   "start": 57.74,
   "end": 64.2
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "ice and I took two of the 200 milligram ibuprofen so 400 twice a day that helps some",
   "start": 64.26,
   "end": 72.32
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "good have you hurt this ankle before",
   "start": 72.32,
   "end": 74.6
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "not this one I sprained my left one in eighth grade but it healed fine no problem since any",
   "start": 74.6,
   "end": 81.84
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "medicines you take every day or any allergies.",
   "start": 81.84,
   "end": 84.32
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Just saidy -razine, 10 milligrams in the spring for my allergies, I'm not on it right now. And I'm allergic to bactrim. I got a rash all over from it.",
   "start": 85.14,
   "end": 94.9
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Got it, sulfa allergy with a rash. Okay, let's take a look. Your blood pressure is 118 over 72, pulse 70. On your right ankle, there's swelling and some bruising on the outside, and your tender right here, in front of the ankle bone on the outside.",
   "start": 95.32,
   "end": 111.24
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yeah, that's the spot.",
   "start": 112.1,
   "end": 112.86
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "No tenderness on the back edge or tip of either ankle bone, and none at the base of your fifth toe bone or on top of the midfoot. When I pull your foot forward, it's a little loose compared to the left, but there's a firm end point. Pulses and feeling in your foot are normal. Can you walk across the room for me?",
   "start": 113.9,
   "end": 131.38
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Sure, it's limpy, but okay.",
   "start": 131.8,
   "end": 133.24
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "You took more than four steps on your own, good. So this is a sprain of the ligaments on the outside of your right ankle, probably grade 1 to 2. Based on the exam, you meet the rules where we don't need an x -ray.",
   "start": 134.16,
   "end": 146.3
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Oh, nice. My friend Diego tore his ACL last month, so my mom kind of freaked out.",
   "start": 147.18,
   "end": 153.16
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Totally understandable, but your knee is fine. Here's the plan. Ice for 15 to 20 minutes every 2 to 3 hours for the next 2 days, keep it up on a pillow, and wear a compression wrap. We'll fit you with a lace -up ankle brace and wear it for practice for the next couple of months. Keep the ibuprofen at 400 milligrams, but every eight hours with food, for five to seven days, then just as needed. You can use crutches for two or three days if walking hurts, but put weight on it as much as you can. And start ankle alphabets, tracing the letters with your toes, a few times a day.",
   "start": 153.7,
   "end": 189.88
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "When can I play again? We've got a tournament in November.",
   "start": 190.66,
   "end": 193.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "No basketball for about two weeks. You can go back once you can hop and run on it without pain. I'll write a note for Coach Brennan and for gym class at Westfield High School. If you can't put weight on it, or the pain moves onto the bone, call us and we'll get an x -ray. If it's not much better in two weeks, come back and we'll set up physical therapy.",
   "start": 194.22,
   "end": 213.92
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Cool. Can you send the note to my portal? My email is kenji .watneb11 at example .com.",
   "start": 214.92,
   "end": 221.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Sure, and the phone number for you is 555 -0192.",
   "start": 222.92,
   "end": 227.28
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yeah, that's my mom's cell.",
   "start": 228.08,
   "end": 229.36
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Perfect. Nice sneakers, by the way.",
   "start": 230.39,
   "end": 232.11
  },
  {
   "idx": 33,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Thanks. They were a birthday present. Wrong ones to roll an ankle in, I guess.",
   "start": 233.05,
   "end": 237.19
  }
 ],
